---
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<!-- Colors are hardcoded (no `dark:` variants) so the footer NEVER changes
     with the light/dark/greyscale toggle — see Header.astro's comment for why. -->
<footer class="border-t border-[#1a3860] bg-[#0c2952] px-4 py-8">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#cbd5e1]">Wager on Weather</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#cbd5e1]">
          Weather intelligence for sports and weather markets. Hourly and 15-day
          forecasts for 41,000+ US ZIP codes and 300+ venues across MLB, NFL,
          NCAA, MLS, and more.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#cbd5e1]">Navigation</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/" class="text-[#cbd5e1] hover:text-[#93c5fd]">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/weatherboard" class="text-[#cbd5e1] hover:text-[#93c5fd]">The Weatherboard</a></li>
          <li><a href="/venues" class="text-[#cbd5e1] hover:text-[#93c5fd]">Venues</a></li>
          <li><a href="/bettheforecast" class="text-[#cbd5e1] hover:text-[#93c5fd]">Bet the Forecast</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#cbd5e1]">Data Sources</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li><span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">Forecasts: produced by Wager on Weather</span></li>
          <li><span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">Observations &amp; market settlement: National Weather Service</span></li>
          <li><span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">Radar: RainViewer &middot; NEXRAD via Iowa State Mesonet</span></li>
          <li><span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">Geocoding: OpenStreetMap Nominatim</span></li>
          <li><span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">Maps: OpenStreetMap &middot; CARTO &middot; Leaflet</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!--
      The "Powered by WeatherNext 2" block was removed 2026-07-29. It credited
      Google DeepMind's WeatherNext 2 and advertised 64 ensemble members at
      0.25-degree resolution, but WeatherNext has never served a customer
      forecast: resolveForecastProvider() defaults to open-meteo, and the
      weathernext paths fail closed with endpoint_unconfirmed and fall back.
      Claiming a model we do not run — on a site people wager against — is a
      misrepresentation, so the whole block and its stats are gone rather than
      reworded.
    -->
    <div class="mt-8 border-t border-[#1a3860] pt-6">
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center text-xs text-[#cbd5e1]">
        Forecasts on this site are produced by Wager on Weather and cover the next
        15 days, hourly for the near term. Weather markets settle on documented
        National Weather Service observations for the stated location and date —
        never on our own forecast.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 border-t border-[#1a3860] pt-4 text-center text-xs text-[#cbd5e1]">
      &copy; {year} Wager on Weather. Weather data is provided for informational purposes only.
      Always follow official weather warnings and local authority guidance.
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
